{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4445877","formula":"Re₂S₇","hill":"Re2S7","elements":["S","Re"],"composition":{"S":7.0,"Re":2.0},"names":{"en":"Rhenium(VII) sulfide","ru":"Сульфид рения(VII)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Rhenium(VII) sulfide is a chemical compound with the formula Re2S7. It has a complex structure, but can be synthesized from direct combination of the elements: 2 Re + 7 S → Δ Re 2 S 7 {\\displaystyle {\\ce {2Re{}+ 7S ->[\\Delta] Re2S7}}} Alternatively, rhenium(VII) oxide reacts with hydrogen sulfide in 4N HCl to the same end: Re 2 O 7 + 7 H 2 S → Δ Re 2 S 7 + 7 H 2 O {\\displaystyle {\\ce {Re2O7{}+ 7H2S ->[\\Delta] Re2S7{}+ 7H2O}}} The compound catalyses the reduction of nitric oxide to nitrous oxide and hydrogenation of double bonds. In this regard, it unusually tolerates sulfur compounds, which poison noble metal catalysts.","ru":"Сульфид рения(VII) — неорганическое соединение, соль металла рения и сероводородной кислоты с формулой Re2S7. Выглядит как нерастворимые в воде чёрно-бурые кристаллы, может образовывать гидраты."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"S=[Re](=S)(=S)S[Re](=S)(=S)=S","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":9,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.374,"y":-1.681,"z":0.59,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.679,"y":-0.061,"z":-0.408,"el":"Re"},{"x":-2.285,"y":1.332,"z":0.777,"el":"S"},{"x":-3.055,"y":-0.397,"z":-1.713,"el":"S"},{"x":0.247,"y":0.633,"z":-1.543,"el":"S"},{"x":1.709,"y":0.139,"z":0.217,"el":"Re"},{"x":2.125,"y":-1.742,"z":0.221,"el":"S"},{"x":3.339,"y":1.126,"z":-0.063,"el":"S"},{"x":0.972,"y":0.65,"z":1.922,"el":"S"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2.0],[1,2,2.0],[1,3,2.0],[1,4,1.0],[4,5,1.0],[5,6,2.0],[5,7,2.0],[5,8,2.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"